                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A light-hearted and indie approach to tower defense games, this one has been released back in 2016 and had a major bug fix some years later so the reviews complaining about game lag and freezes are luckily no more valid under this aspect.\nStill, this game has had very few players and reviews and it seems that the developers, who had planned to translate the game into other languages apart from English, are no more active. Hence, I think this game won't ever be upgraded anymore and they won't probably release anything else, given their total inactivity.\nThe game features a nice sci-fi space graphics, with the levels taking place into spaceships; it flows like a very classical tower defense game: we'll have a top-down gameplay screen, some turrets with different abilities, a fixed trail which the enemies will follow in order to travel from the start to the core of your ship. There's also another box containing the information regarding hp, money, number of waves and such.\nClicking on a tower makes a small information box appear, telling us its cost, damage and a brief description of its characteristics. Obviously, you can upgrade them.\nAnd there's the usual speed up button!\nApart from the sci-fi setting, this game is definitely a classic tower defense game - it features no innovations at all. We'll have to place our towers in order to create some kind of maze, let the enemies go through and kill them while keeping an eye on money, lives and such.\nIf you like tower defense games, this one even if it's quite old it's still a solid indie title. Just don't expect a masterpiece, it's just your average TD game with all its mandatory features - various towers, upgrades, enemy waves and so on. If it's among your genres, it has no bugs right now and it's quite enjoyable.\n",
